  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acute Crises Joint Response for Flood Affected Victim in Jere and MMC LGAs Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;In Borno state in Nigeria, a flash flooding&amp;nbsp; occurred on the night of 9 September 2024, when the Alau Dam collapsed, causing widespread flooding across the state capital Maiduguri, Jere and Konduga local government areas (LGAs), affecting more than 1 million people and resulting in more than 400 deaths. More than 414,000 people, mostly IDPs have been registered in 30 relocation sites, following evacuations from flood affected areas.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;ZOA and its partner provide life-saving WASH and&amp;nbsp; MPC support to the most affected people in the relocation camps.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
