     <period-end iso-date="2025-02-20"></period-end>
     <target value="1"></target>
     <actual value="5">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.There was a shift from the conventional hygiene promotion key messages to the inclusion of training of participants in liquid soap production.2.Inclusion of sensitization of mobile water vendors for safe water hygiene in the project.3.Water trucking in IDP camp (Gubio IDP camp)4.Vendors integrated community members in the construction and rehabilitation of WASH facilities5. LHI implemented IYCF sessions and food demonstrations to 1320 (14 males, 1,306 females). They also conducted livelihood trainings to 2000 individuals that received the MPC one-off support. The trainings were on small scale business enterprises, financial literacy, conflict management, SIYB (Start, improve your business) and EYH (enterprise your household)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
